Usage: man [OPTION]... [COMMAND]...

Display manual page for a WinuxCmd command.
[DIFFERS] Options -t, -T, -H are GNU-specific and not available on Windows.

OPTIONS:
  -l, --list          list all available commands
  -w, --where         print physical location of manual page
  -P, --pager ARG     use program PAGER to display output
  -t, --troff         use groff to format pages [DIFFERS: not available on
                      Windows]
  -T, --troff-device  use groff with selected device [DIFFERS: not available on
                      Windows]
  -H, --html          display HTML output [DIFFERS: not available on Windows]
      --help          display this help and exit
  -V, --version       output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
